          {
            "name": "What makes Formester form management software different from a form builder?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Form builders focus on making one form. Form management software focuses on operating a library of forms at scale: multiple team members, role-based access, workflow rules, submission routing, centralized reporting, API access. Formester ships both: the builder for creating forms and the management layer (Workspaces, roles, rules, API) for running them at team scale.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "How does Formester compare to Formstack for form management?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Formstack starts at $50/user/month and adds up quickly at 5+ seats. Formester's Business plan is $49/month TOTAL for 25 team seats, unlimited forms, unlimited responses, workflow rules, and API access. Formstack ships HIPAA compliance and PCI Level 1 as its main differentiator. If HIPAA or PCI Level 1 is a hard requirement, Formstack. Everything else, Formester at 5-10% of the cost.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Is there a free plan?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Yes. Formester's free plan has unlimited forms and unlimited responses. No trial. No credit card. Native payment collection, AI form generator, custom email notifications, quiz auto-scoring, and drop-off analytics all included on free. Paid plans (Personal $13/mo, Business $49/mo) unlock branding removal, conditional logic, API access, team seats, and PDF export.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Can I self-host Formester?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Not today. Formester is hosted only. If self-hosting is a hard requirement (data sovereignty, air-gapped networks), Form.io ships a self-hostable version. Formester's hosted infrastructure is on AWS with GDPR-compliant regional hosting available.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "How does Formester's MCP server work?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Point Claude Desktop, Cursor, or any MCP-compatible AI client at Formester's MCP server URL. The AI can then create forms, list forms, fetch submissions, and update forms using your Formester API credentials. Same permissions as your account. Ideal for teams that want to author forms from a chat interface.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "What about workflow automations?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Formester ships native rules: route submissions by field value, tag by source, notify the right owner, escalate by threshold. For deeper workflows (multi-step approvals, external system triggers, complex branching), use the native Zapier integration (500+ apps) or webhooks.",
